ove me right.\"},\"reference_example\":\"Fact: The investment has fallen. You still believe in the original thesis. Some sources support your view. Other information challenges it. You are considering adding more money.\\nStory: The market is wrong. If I buy more now, the recovery will prove me right.\"},{\"step_number\":2,\"key\":\"decode\",\"prompt\":\"Which thinking trap(s) may be influencing your judgment? Select the one you think is primary and note any others.\",\"input_type\":\"single_choice_with_multi_notes\",\"options\":[{\"key\":\"mind_reading\",\"label\":\"Mind Reading\",\"definition\":\"Assuming others\' intentions without evidence.\"},{\"key\":\"fortune_telling\",\"label\":\"Fortune Telling\",\"definition\":\"Treating an unverified prediction as certain.\"},{\"key\":\"emotional_reasoning\",\"label\":\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"definition\":\"Treating a feeling as proof of reality.\"},{\"key\":\"catastrophizing\",\"label\":\"Catastrophizing\",\"definition\":\"Assuming the absolute worst outcome.\"},{\"key\":\"confirmation_bias\",\"label\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"definition\":\"Only seeing details that confirm the feared story.\"},{\"key\":\"rumination\",\"label\":\"Rumination\",\"definition\":\"Repetitive, circular overthinking of past events.\"},{\"key\":\"all_or_nothing\",\"label\":\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\",\"definition\":\"Treating a minor gap as total failure or framing as either-or.\"},{\"key\":\"validation_seeking\",\"label\":\"Validation Seeking\",\"definition\":\"Allowing external approval to define self-worth or decisions.\"},{\"key\":\"sunk_cost_fallacy\",\"label\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"definition\":\"Continuing a path solely because of past unrecoverable investment.\"}],\"correct_option_key\":\"confirmation_bias\",\"primary_trap\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Fortune Telling\",\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\"],\"secondary_trap_keys\":[\"fortune_telling\",\"sunk_cost_fallacy\"],\"explanation_reveal\":\"after_commit\",\"explanation\":\"Confirmation Bias can make supportive information easier to notice. Sunk Cost can make the existing investment feel like a reason to continue. Fortune Telling can turn an expected recovery into a certainty.\\nRemember: More than one thinking trap can exist in the same situation. The goal is not to label yourself; it is to identify what may be distorting the decision.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"prompt\":\"Answer these questions before deciding what the situation means:\\n• What facts do you know for certain?\\n• What assumptions are you making?\\n• What evidence supports your conclusion?\\n• What evidence challenges it?\\n• What information is still missing?\",\"tip\":\"Missing information is not evidence. Identify what you would need to know before becoming more certain.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What facts do you know for certain?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. What assumptions are you making?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q3\",\"prompt\":\"3. What evidence supports your conclusion?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q4\",\"prompt\":\"4. What evidence challenges it?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q5\",\"prompt\":\"5. What information is still missing?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"The price decline is real.\",\"The original thesis may or may not still hold.\",\"Past investment does not justify a new investment by itself.\",\"A future recovery is uncertain.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"The price decline is real.\",\"The original thesis may or may not still hold.\",\"Past investment does not justify a new investment by itself.\",\"A future recovery is uncertain.\"]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"prompt\":\"Generate at least four plausible alternatives. At least one should challenge your first interpretation.\",\"insight\":\"Reframing does not mean forcing a positive interpretation. It means expanding the set of explanations or options before deciding.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"alt_explanations\",\"prompt\":\"Write at least four other explanations or perspectives that also fit the facts.\",\"type\":\"multi_entry\",\"min_entries\":4}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"The original thesis may still be valid.\",\"The business fundamentals may have changed.\",\"The decline may reflect broader market conditions.\",\"There may be better uses for additional capital.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"The original thesis may still be valid.\",\"The business fundamentals may have changed.\",\"The decline may reflect broader market conditions.\",\"There may be better uses for additional capital.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"prompt\":\"Choose one reasonable next action. Explain what it will help you learn, clarify or protect.\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action. There is usually a reasonable next action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"Based on the evidence available today, what is the most reasonable next action?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Reassess the business using current information as if you did not already own it.\",\"Define what evidence would invalidate the original thesis.\",\"Do not add capital solely to reduce the psychological discomfort of a loss.\"],\"reference_example\":\"Reassess the business using current information as if you did not already own it.\\nDefine what evidence would invalidate the original thesis.\\nDo not add capital solely to reduce the psychological discomfort of a loss.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “Today I learned that…”\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “Today I learned that…”\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":\"A new investment deserves a fresh decision, even when I already own the asset.\",\"reference_example\":\"A new investment deserves a fresh decision, even when I already own the asset.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"If you did not own this investment today, would the current evidence make you buy it?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional reflection entry — take a moment to reflect on today\'s scenario.\",\"required\":false}}}', `updated_at` = '2026-09-25 16:36:12';

INSERT INTO `foundation_days` (`day_number`, `phase`, `title`, `domain`, `primary_trap`, `secondary_trap`, `content_bundle`, `created_at`, `updated_at`)
VALUES (30, 2, 'The Partner Disagreement', 'Business', 'Mind Reading', 'Emotional Reasoning, Confirmation Bias', '{\"day\":30,\"phase\":2,\"title\":\"The Partner Disagreement\",\"domain\":\"Business\",\"mission\":\"Conflict does not automatically reveal intent.\",\"learning_objective\":\"Choose Thoughtful Actions\",\"difficulty\":\"Intermediate\",\"emotional_intensity\":\"Moderate\",\"estimated_minutes\":\"4-6\",\"primary_skill\":\"Intervention\",\"primary_trap\":\"Mind Reading\",\"secondary_trap\":\"Emotional Reasoning, Confirmation Bias\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"Confirmation Bias\"],\"guidance_level\":\"Moderate-to-reduced guidance; user must defend the next action and work with competing information.\",\"interaction_principle\":\"Think → Commit → Defend → Compare → Reflect\",\"scenario_text\":\"You and your business partner disagree about expanding into a new market.\\nYour partner rejects your proposal in a short meeting.\\nYou feel dismissed.\\nLater, you hear that the partner discussed the expansion with another colleague.\\nYou start thinking that your partner no longer trusts you and may be planning to make decisions without you.\",\"steps\":[{\"step_number\":1,\"key\":\"detect\",\"prompt\":\"Before you interpret the situation, identify the facts, then state the story or conclusion your mind is moving toward.\",\"insight\":\"Facts describe what is known. The story explains what the mind thinks the facts mean.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"facts\",\"prompt\":\"Write only the facts.\",\"multiline\":true},{\"field_key\":\"story\",\"prompt\":\"Now write the story\\/assumptions your mind is creating.\",\"multiline\":true}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":{\"facts\":[\"Your proposal was rejected.\",\"The discussion was brief.\",\"You felt dismissed.\",\"Your partner discussed the expansion with another colleague.\",\"You do not know what was discussed.\"],\"story\":\"My partner no longer trusts me and is going around me.\"},\"reference_example\":\"Fact: Your proposal was rejected. The discussion was brief. You felt dismissed. Your partner discussed the expansion with another colleague. You do not know what was discussed.\\nStory: My partner no longer trusts me and is going around me.\"},{\"step_number\":2,\"key\":\"decode\",\"prompt\":\"Which thinking trap(s) may be influencing your judgment? Select the one you think is primary and note any others.\",\"input_type\":\"single_choice_with_multi_notes\",\"options\":[{\"key\":\"mind_reading\",\"label\":\"Mind Reading\",\"definition\":\"Assuming others\' intentions without evidence.\"},{\"key\":\"fortune_telling\",\"label\":\"Fortune Telling\",\"definition\":\"Treating an unverified prediction as certain.\"},{\"key\":\"emotional_reasoning\",\"label\":\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"definition\":\"Treating a feeling as proof of reality.\"},{\"key\":\"catastrophizing\",\"label\":\"Catastrophizing\",\"definition\":\"Assuming the absolute worst outcome.\"},{\"key\":\"confirmation_bias\",\"label\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"definition\":\"Only seeing details that confirm the feared story.\"},{\"key\":\"rumination\",\"label\":\"Rumination\",\"definition\":\"Repetitive, circular overthinking of past events.\"},{\"key\":\"all_or_nothing\",\"label\":\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\",\"definition\":\"Treating a minor gap as total failure or framing as either-or.\"},{\"key\":\"validation_seeking\",\"label\":\"Validation Seeking\",\"definition\":\"Allowing external approval to define self-worth or decisions.\"},{\"key\":\"sunk_cost_fallacy\",\"label\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"definition\":\"Continuing a path solely because of past unrecoverable investment.\"}],\"correct_option_key\":\"mind_reading\",\"primary_trap\":\"Mind Reading\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"Confirmation Bias\"],\"secondary_trap_keys\":[\"emotional_reasoning\",\"confirmation_bias\"],\"explanation_reveal\":\"after_commit\",\"explanation\":\"Mind Reading infers intent from limited behaviour. Emotional Reasoning makes the feeling of being dismissed feel like proof. Confirmation Bias can cause later events to be interpreted as evidence of the same story.\\nRemember: More than one thinking trap can exist in the same situation. The goal is not to label yourself; it is to identify what may be distorting the decision.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"prompt\":\"Answer these questions before deciding what the situation means:\\n• What facts do you know for certain?\\n• What assumptions are you making?\\n• What evidence supports your conclusion?\\n• What evidence challenges it?\\n• What information is still missing?\",\"tip\":\"Missing information is not evidence. Identify what you would need to know before becoming more certain.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What facts do you know for certain?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. What assumptions are you making?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q3\",\"prompt\":\"3. What evidence supports your conclusion?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q4\",\"prompt\":\"4. What evidence challenges it?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q5\",\"prompt\":\"5. What information is still missing?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"The proposal was rejected.\",\"The reason is not fully understood.\",\"A separate conversation occurred.\",\"There is no evidence yet that the partner intends to exclude you.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"The proposal was rejected.\",\"The reason is not fully understood.\",\"A separate conversation occurred.\",\"There is no evidence yet that the partner intends to exclude you.\"]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"prompt\":\"Generate at least four plausible alternatives. At least one should challenge your first interpretation.\",\"insight\":\"Reframing does not mean forcing a positive interpretation. It means expanding the set of explanations or options before deciding.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"alt_explanations\",\"prompt\":\"Write at least four other explanations or perspectives that also fit the facts.\",\"type\":\"multi_entry\",\"min_entries\":4}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"The partner wanted another perspective.\",\"The partner had concerns about the proposal itself.\",\"The discussion may have been operational rather than personal.\",\"There may be a communication problem rather than a trust problem.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"The partner wanted another perspective.\",\"The partner had concerns about the proposal itself.\",\"The discussion may have been operational rather than personal.\",\"There may be a communication problem rather than a trust problem.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"prompt\":\"Choose one reasonable next action. Explain what it will help you learn, clarify or protect.\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action. There is usually a reasonable next action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"Based on the evidence available today, what is the most reasonable next action?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Have a direct conversation focused on the decision and roles.\",\"Ask what concerns led to the rejection.\",\"Clarify how major decisions should be discussed between partners.\"],\"reference_example\":\"Have a direct conversation focused on the decision and roles.\\nAsk what concerns led to the rejection.\\nClarify how major decisions should be discussed between partners.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “Today I learned that…”\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “Today I learned that…”\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":\"I can address a relationship problem without first deciding what the other person intended.\",\"reference_example\":\"I can address a relationship problem without first deciding what the other person intended.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"When you feel dismissed, do you ask for clarification or immediately assign an intention?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional reflection entry — take a moment to reflect on today\'s scenario.\",\"required\":false}}}', '2026-09-25 16:36:12', '2026-09-25 16:36:12')
