dation Seeking\"],\"secondary_trap_keys\":[\"sunk_cost_fallacy\",\"validation_seeking\"],\"explanation_reveal\":\"after_commit\",\"explanation\":\"All-or-Nothing Thinking can turn a trade-off into a search for one universally correct answer. Validation Seeking can overweight prestige. Sunk Cost may make you protect the career path already built.\\nRemember: More than one thinking trap can exist in the same situation. The goal is not to label yourself; it is to identify what may be distorting the decision.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"prompt\":\"Build your own reality check. Identify the facts, assumptions, evidence for and against your view, and the missing information that could materially change the decision.\",\"tip\":\"Missing information is not evidence. Identify what you would need to know before becoming more certain.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What facts do you know for certain?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. What assumptions are you making?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q3\",\"prompt\":\"3. What evidence supports your conclusion?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q4\",\"prompt\":\"4. What evidence challenges it?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q5\",\"prompt\":\"5. What information is still missing?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"The options optimize different things.\",\"There is no evidence that one factor should automatically dominate.\",\"The opportunity cost of each option matters.\",\"The right decision depends on current priorities and constraints.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"The options optimize different things.\",\"There is no evidence that one factor should automatically dominate.\",\"The opportunity cost of each option matters.\",\"The right decision depends on current priorities and constraints.\"]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"prompt\":\"Generate the realistic alternatives available to you. Include at least one option that is not your preferred choice and, where relevant, an option that changes the structure of the decision rather than simply choosing A or B.\",\"insight\":\"A decision can improve when you change the question from “Which option wins?” to “What options, conditions or safeguards could make the decision better?”\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"alt_explanations\",\"prompt\":\"Write at least four other explanations or perspectives that also fit the facts.\",\"type\":\"multi_entry\",\"min_entries\":4}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Choose income and stability now.\",\"Choose domain transition and long-term learning.\",\"Negotiate the role to improve the trade-off.\",\"Delay if neither option fits the current constraints.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"Choose income and stability now.\",\"Choose domain transition and long-term learning.\",\"Negotiate the role to improve the trade-off.\",\"Delay if neither option fits the current constraints.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"prompt\":\"What would you do next, and why? If this is a decision rather than an immediate reaction, state what information, negotiation, experiment or safeguard should come before the final commitment.\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action. There is usually a reasonable next action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"Based on the evidence available today, what is the most reasonable next action?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Define the 3–4 outcomes that matter most for the next few years.\",\"Compare what each option gives and what it costs.\",\"Make the trade-off explicit rather than searching for a perfect option.\"],\"reference_example\":\"Define the 3–4 outcomes that matter most for the next few years.\\nCompare what each option gives and what it costs.\\nMake the trade-off explicit rather than searching for a perfect option.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “The judgment principle I want to carry forward is…”\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “Today I learned that…”\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":\"A good decision can still involve giving something up. Judgment means choosing the trade-off deliberately.\",\"reference_example\":\"A good decision can still involve giving something up. Judgment means choosing the trade-off deliberately.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"What are you unwilling to give up—and what does that tell you about your priorities?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional reflection entry — take a moment to reflect on today\'s scenario.\",\"required\":false}}}', `updated_at` = '2026-09-25 16:36:12';

INSERT INTO `foundation_days` (`day_number`, `phase`, `title`, `domain`, `primary_trap`, `secondary_trap`, `content_bundle`, `created_at`, `updated_at`)
VALUES (39, 2, 'The Struggling Unit', 'Leadership', 'Confirmation Bias', 'Catastrophizing, Sunk Cost Fallacy', '{\"day\":39,\"phase\":2,\"title\":\"The Struggling Unit\",\"domain\":\"Leadership\",\"mission\":\"The hardest decisions rarely depend on one variable.\",\"learning_objective\":\"Integrate Multi-Variable Judgment\",\"difficulty\":\"Intermediate–Advanced\",\"emotional_intensity\":\"High\",\"estimated_minutes\":\"5-7\",\"primary_skill\":\"Reality Check\",\"primary_trap\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"secondary_trap\":\"Catastrophizing, Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Catastrophizing\",\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\"],\"guidance_level\":\"Low guidance; multi-variable judgment, competing values and uncertainty are central.\",\"interaction_principle\":\"Think → Commit → Defend → Compare → Reflect\",\"scenario_text\":\"You are asked to stabilize an underperforming business unit.\\nThe unit has a strong brand and a loyal customer base but has lost money for two years.\\nThe owners want growth.\\nThe team is already stretched.\\nA turnaround requires investment, leadership changes and time, but there is no guarantee of success.\\nYou have authority to recommend a path, but not to make the final investment decision.\",\"steps\":[{\"step_number\":1,\"key\":\"detect\",\"prompt\":\"Start without looking for the \'right\' answer. Write what you know, what you think it means, and what you are tempted to do.\",\"insight\":\"Facts describe what is known. The story explains what the mind thinks the facts mean.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"facts\",\"prompt\":\"Write only the facts.\",\"multiline\":true},{\"field_key\":\"story\",\"prompt\":\"Now write the story\\/assumptions your mind is creating.\",\"multiline\":true}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":{\"facts\":[\"The unit has a strong brand and customer base.\",\"It has lost money for two years.\",\"The team is stretched.\",\"A turnaround requires investment and changes.\",\"Success is uncertain.\",\"Final investment approval belongs to the owners.\"],\"story\":\"The brand is too valuable to give up; we just need to push harder.\"},\"reference_example\":\"Fact: The unit has a strong brand and customer base. It has lost money for two years. The team is stretched. A turnaround requires investment and changes. Success is uncertain. Final investment approval belongs to the owners.\\nStory: The brand is too valuable to give up; we just need to push harder.\"},{\"step_number\":2,\"key\":\"decode\",\"prompt\":\"Which thinking trap(s) may be influencing your judgment? Select the one you think is primary and note any others.\",\"input_type\":\"single_choice_with_multi_notes\",\"options\":[{\"key\":\"mind_reading\",\"label\":\"Mind Reading\",\"definition\":\"Assuming others\' intentions without evidence.\"},{\"key\":\"fortune_telling\",\"label\":\"Fortune Telling\",\"definition\":\"Treating an unverified prediction as certain.\"},{\"key\":\"emotional_reasoning\",\"label\":\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"definition\":\"Treating a feeling as proof of reality.\"},{\"key\":\"catastrophizing\",\"label\":\"Catastrophizing\",\"definition\":\"Assuming the absolute worst outcome.\"},{\"key\":\"confirmation_bias\",\"label\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"definition\":\"Only seeing details that confirm the feared story.\"},{\"key\":\"rumination\",\"label\":\"Rumination\",\"definition\":\"Repetitive, circular overthinking of past events.\"},{\"key\":\"all_or_nothing\",\"label\":\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\",\"definition\":\"Treating a minor gap as total failure or framing as either-or.\"},{\"key\":\"validation_seeking\",\"label\":\"Validation Seeking\",\"definition\":\"Allowing external approval to define self-worth or decisions.\"},{\"key\":\"sunk_cost_fallacy\",\"label\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"definition\":\"Continuing a path solely because of past unrecoverable investment.\"}],\"correct_option_key\":\"confirmation_bias\",\"primary_trap\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Catastrophizing\",\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\"],\"secondary_trap_keys\":[\"catastrophizing\",\"sunk_cost_fallacy\"],\"explanation_reveal\":\"after_commit\",\"explanation\":\"Confirmation Bias can overvalue the brand and loyal customers while underweighting the financial evidence. Sunk Cost can make past investment feel like a reason to continue. Catastrophizing may also appear if stopping is framed as catastrophic failure.\\nRemember: More than one thinking trap can exist in the same situation. The goal is not to label yourself; it is to identify what may be distorting the decision.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"prompt\":\"Build your own reality check. Identify the facts, assumptions, evidence for and against your view, and the missing information that could materially change the decision.\",\"tip\":\"Missing information is not evidence. Identify what you would need to know before becoming more certain.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What facts do you know for certain?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. What assumptions are you making?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q3\",\"prompt\":\"3. What evidence supports your conclusion?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q4\",\"prompt\":\"4. What evidence challenges it?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q5\",\"prompt\":\"5. What information is still missing?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"The brand has value.\",\"The current model has not produced sustainable financial performance.\",\"The turnaround requires additional resources.\",\"The decision depends on whether a credible path to sustainability exists.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"The brand has value.\",\"The current model has not produced sustainable financial performance.\",\"The turnaround requires additional resources.\",\"The decision depends on whether a credible path to sustainability exists.\"]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"prompt\":\"Generate the realistic alternatives available to you. Include at least one option that is not your preferred choice and, where relevant, an option that changes the structure of the decision rather than simply choosing A or B.\",\"insight\":\"A decision can improve when you change the question from “Which option wins?” to “What options, conditions or safeguards could make the decision better?”\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"alt_explanations\",\"prompt\":\"Write at least four other explanations or perspectives that also fit the facts.\",\"type\":\"multi_entry\",\"min_entries\":4}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Continue with a defined turnaround plan.\",\"Restructure the unit before investing further.\",\"Reduce the scope and test a focused model.\",\"Exit or redeploy resources if the economics cannot be repaired.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"Continue with a defined turnaround plan.\",\"Restructure the unit before investing further.\",\"Reduce the scope and test a focused model.\",\"Exit or redeploy resources if the economics cannot be repaired.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"prompt\":\"What would you do next, and why? If this is a decision rather than an immediate reaction, state what information, negotiation, experiment or safeguard should come before the final commitment.\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action. There is usually a reasonable next action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"Based on the evidence available today, what is the most reasonable next action?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Build scenarios with explicit assumptions, milestones and stop criteria.\",\"Identify what evidence would show the turnaround is working.\",\"Present the options and trade-offs to the owners rather than advocating from attachment to the past.\"],\"reference_example\":\"Build scenarios with explicit assumptions, milestones and stop criteria.\\nIdentify what evidence would show the turnaround is working.\\nPresent the options and trade-offs to the owners rather than advocating from attachment to the past.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “The judgment principle I want to carry forward is…”\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “Today I learned that…”\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":\"A valuable asset can still require a different strategy. Good judgment tests whether the future case is strong enough.\",\"reference_example\":\"A valuable asset can still require a different strategy. Good judgment tests whether the future case is strong enough.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"Which fact would most change your view of this situation?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional reflection entry — take a moment to reflect on today\'s scenario.\",\"required\":false}}}', '2026-09-25 16:36:12', '2026-09-25 16:36:12')
